[38;2;124;124;124mI think the pattern is clear. Let me now try to prove this rigorously by strong [0m[38;2;124;124;124minduction.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Claim:** In Case 2, $f(n)=n$ for all $n\in\mathbb{Z}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Approach:** Use strong induction. Suppose $f(k)=k$ for all $|k|\leq N$. Show [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$f(N+1)=N+1$ and $f(-(N+1))=-(N+1)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe key equation is $(\star)$: $2f(a^2+b^2)-2f(ab)=f(a-b)^2+f(a)^2+f(b)^2$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mIf $|a|,|b|,|a-b|\leq N$, then $f(a^2+b^2)=ab+\frac{(a-b)^2+a^2+b^2}{2}[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m=a^2+b^2$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo we can determine $f(a^2+b^2)$ whenever $|a|,|b|,|a-b|\leq N$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSimilarly, from the original equation, if $|a|,|b|,|c|,|a-b|,|b-c|,|c-a|\leq N$,[0m[38;2;124;124;124mthen $f(a^2+b^2+c^2)=a^2+b^2+c^2$ (given $f(ab+bc+ca)=ab+bc+ca$, which requires [0m[38;2;124;124;124m$|ab+bc+ca|\leq N$).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mHmm, this is getting complicated because we need $ab+bc+ca$ to also be within [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthe range.[0m

