[38;2;124;124;124mThis is getting complicated. Let me try yet another approach.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Key idea:** Let me try to show $f$ is determined by $f(1)$ and that [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$f(n)=n\cdot f(1)$ for all $n$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mIf $f(n)=cn$ for some constant $c$, then $f(n^2)=cn^2$ and $f(n)^2=c^2n^2$. From[0m[38;2;124;124;124m$f(n^2)=f(n)^2$: $cn^2=c^2n^2$, so $c=c^2$, giving $c=0$ or $c=1$.[0m

